title: AWS v2: Agent info
agents: aws_v2
catalog: cloud/aws
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check shows what one run of the AWS special agent reached.

 It counts the accounts the agent monitored. It goes CRIT for each
 account the agent could not reach, for example because the role in
 that account cannot be assumed, and for a failed login. The service
 details show the reason.

 Regions an account has not enabled and sections a service control
 policy denies are shown as information. They do not change the state.

 To make this check work you have to configure the related
 special agent {Amazon Web Services (AWS) v2}.

discovery:
 One service is created on the host of the special agent rule.
